.TH iron-vault-approver 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-approver \- Manage the approvers that sign configuration approvals
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault approver\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the approvers that sign configuration approvals
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
iron\-vault\-approver\-list(1)
List every approver, one line each: its approver ID, signer kind, enrolment time, `active` when it signed the active approval, and label. The first line is the approver a prompt asks first. It works while the service is Ready
.TP
iron\-vault\-approver\-add(1)
Enroll another approval signer. The service shows what changes, asks for the approval passphrase of an approver already pinned, then for the new signer\*(Aqs own approval passphrase, twice; choose one different from the vault passphrase. The new signer alone can approve a config, so keep its passphrase apart from the first. Prints the new approver\*(Aqs ID
